    "source_location_status": "EXACT_SOURCE_QUOTATION",
    "source_excerpts": [
      {
        "line_start": 327,
        "line_end": 334,
        "excerpt": "Restrictions on draughts when operating in ice shall be documented and kept on board readily\navailable to the master. The maximum and minimum ice class draughts fore, amidships and aft\nshall be indicated in the class certificate. For ships built on or after 1 July 2007, if the summer\nload line in fresh water is anywhere located at a higher level than the UIWL, the ship’s sides\nare to be provided with a warning triangle and with an ice class draught mark at the maximum\npermissible ice class draught amidships (see Annex III). Ships built before 1 July 2007 shall be\nprovided with such a marking, if the UIWL is below the summer load line, not later than the\nfirst scheduled dry docking after 1 July 2007."
      }
    ]
